---
/**
 * Tokens lesson — illustration #3 of 3.
 *
 * One BPE merge step, before-and-after, with the (e, r) pair
 * highlighted in red on the left and the merged "er" token
 * highlighted in green on the right.
 *
 * Why this diagram:
 *   The text already shows the corpus before and after in code blocks,
 *   but the highlighting (which pairs got merged) is what the prose
 *   describes and the eye misses without color. This makes the merge
 *   visible at a glance.
 */
---

<figure class="cw-illus">
	<svg viewBox="0 0 800 280" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-labelledby="bpe-title bpe-desc">
		<title id="bpe-title">One byte-pair encoding merge step</title>
		<desc id="bpe-desc">Two corpus listings side by side. On the left, "before" the merge: each occurrence of the pair (e, r) is highlighted in red. On the right, "after" the merge: each (e, r) has been replaced by a single new token "er", highlighted in green. The vocabulary just grew by one entry.</desc>
		<text x="160" y="30" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="600" fill="currentColor">before</text>
		<text x="640" y="30" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="14" font-weight="600" fill="currentColor">after</text>
		<text x="40" y="70" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="14" fill="currentColor">{"l o w </w>        (5)"}</text>
		<text x="40" y="95" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="14" fill="currentColor">{"l o w "}<tspan fill="#dc2626" font-weight="700">{"e r"}</tspan>{" </w>    (2)"}</text>
		<text x="40" y="120" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="14" fill="currentColor">{"n e w "}<tspan fill="#dc2626" font-weight="700">{"e r"}</tspan>{" </w>    (6)"}</text>
		<text x="40" y="145" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="14" fill="currentColor">{"w i d "}<tspan fill="#dc2626" font-weight="700">{"e r"}</tspan>{" </w>    (3)"}</text>
		<text x="40" y="170" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="14" fill="currentColor">{"n e w </w>        (1)"}</text>
		<defs>
			<marker id="cw-arrow-3" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto">
				<path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill="#7c3aed"/>
			</marker>
		</defs>
		<line x1="335" y1="118" x2="465" y2="118" stroke="#7c3aed" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#cw-arrow-3)"/>
		<text x="400" y="105" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="600" fill="#7c3aed">merge</text>
		<text x="400" y="138" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.7">11 occurrences,</text>
		<text x="400" y="153" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.7">the most frequent pair</text>
		<text x="490" y="70" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="14" fill="currentColor">{"l o w </w>        (5)"}</text>
		<text x="490" y="95" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="14" fill="currentColor">{"l o w "}<tspan fill="#16a34a" font-weight="700">{"er"}</tspan>{" </w>     (2)"}</text>
		<text x="490" y="120" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="14" fill="currentColor">{"n e w "}<tspan fill="#16a34a" font-weight="700">{"er"}</tspan>{" </w>     (6)"}</text>
		<text x="490" y="145" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="14" fill="currentColor">{"w i d "}<tspan fill="#16a34a" font-weight="700">{"er"}</tspan>{" </w>     (3)"}</text>
		<text x="490" y="170" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="14" fill="currentColor">{"n e w </w>        (1)"}</text>
		<text x="400" y="230" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.75">the vocabulary just grew by one entry: <tspan font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-weight="700" fill="#16a34a">er</tspan></text>
	</svg>
	<figcaption>One BPE merge: the pair (e, r) appears more often than any other adjacent pair across this tiny corpus, so it gets fused into a new vocabulary entry "er". Repeat the same loop 50,000 times for a real vocabulary.</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
	.cw-illus {
		margin: 1.75rem auto;
		max-width: 100%;
	}
	.cw-illus svg {
		display: block;
		width: 100%;
		max-width: 780px;
		height: auto;
		margin: 0 auto;
	}
	.cw-illus figcaption {
		text-align: center;
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		opacity: 0.75;
		margin-top: 0.5rem;
		font-style: italic;
	}
</style>
